peech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)\n,\nCited by:\n§5.1\n,\n§5.2\n.\n[21]\nUniversal Music Group\n(2025-Oct.)\nUniversal Music Group and Stability AI Announce Strategic Alliance to Co-Develop Professional AI Music Creation Tools\n.\nNote:\nPress ReleaseAccessed on July 2026\nExternal Links:\nLink\nCited by:\n§1\n.\n[22]\nWarner Music Group\n(2025-Nov.)\nWarner Music Group and Stability AI Join Forces to Build the Next Generation of Responsible AI Tools for Music Creation\n.\nNote:\nPress ReleaseAccessed on July 2026\nExternal Links:\nLink\nCited by:\n§1\n.\n[23]\nWarner Music Group\n(2025-Nov.)\nWarner Music Group and Suno Forge Groundbreaking Partnership\n.\nNote:\nPress ReleaseAccessed on July 2026\nExternal Links:\nLink\nCited by:\n§1\n.\n[24]\nZ. Yin, F. Reuben, S. Stepney, and T. Collins\n(2022)\nMeasuring when a music generation algorithm copies too much: the originality report, cardinality score, and symbolic fingerprinting by geometric hashing\n.\nSN Computer Science\n3\n(\n5\n),\npp. 340\n.\nCited by:\n§1\n.\n[25]\nY. Zang, Y. Zhang, M. Heydari, and Z. Duan\n(2024)\nSingfake: Singing voice deepfake detection\n.\nIn\nProc. of the IEEE Int. Conf. on Acoustics, Speech and Signal Processing (ICASSP)\n,\nCited by:\n§2\n.\nExperimental support, please\nview the build logs\nfor errors. Generated by\nL\nA\nT\nE\nxml\n.\nInstructions for reporting errors\nWe are continuing to improve HTML versions of papers, and your feedback helps enhance accessibility and mobile\n      support. To report errors in the HTML that will help us improve conversion and rendering, choose any of the\n      methods listed below:\nClick the \"Report Issue\"\n(\n)\nbutton, located in the page header.\nTip:\nYou can select the relevant text first, to include it in your report.\nOur team has already identified\nthe following issues\n. We appreciate your time reviewing and reporting rendering errors we\n      may not have found yet. Your efforts will help us improve the HTML versions for all r